WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.660
As I'm taping this right this right now, there's
a massive fire burning about 70 miles north

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.959
of here in Ventura County.

00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:16.950
As of a few minutes ago it had already burned
over 50,000 acres and over 30,000 homes have

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.090
been evacuated.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.419
I'm sure by the time you see this video those
numbers will go up significantly.

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:27.400
Here in Los Angeles there's soot flying around
everywhere and there's a dark grey haze and

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.430
a deep smell of smoke.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:33.210
I just walked my dog for literally 2 minutes
and not only couldn't I see all the way down

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.200
to the end of the block because of smoke,
but my clothes stink right now.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.270
Fortunately YouTube hasn't given us access
to their smell--o-vision feature just yet.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:42.129
We just finished up our interview for this
week with Jessica Flanigan from the University

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:48.660
of Richmond and although we never edit for
content, we're probably gonna edit out a couple

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.320
coughs and hacks as the air quality in the
studio is pretty bad right now.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.989
Ironically our interview had a lot to do with
public health, so stay tuned for that.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:01.739
I don't mention any of this for pity for me
dealing with some soot and smoke today as

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:05.890
much as how things can be put into perspective
pretty quickly.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.790
Of course a quick perusal of Twitter allowed
me to see people saying California was burning

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:14.050
because of its leftists sins and others saying
it's burning because of global warming and

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.180
lack of regulation.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.410
Yes, even natural disasters are political
these days.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.480
As we're in the midst of the holiday season
perhaps let's try to be a little less political

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.940
as we run out 2017.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:31.060
The spirit of the season is about joy and
giving, not fighting and bickering, and it

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.740
seems we do the latter two a lot more often
than the former two these days.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.790
The people being affected far worse than me
by these fires are on the left and the right,

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:45.650
they're pro-choice and pro-life, they're black
and white and Christian and atheist.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:51.130
It's not just good ideas that can bring us
together, but also bad events, so let's not

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.600
make them worse with an extra helping of hate.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.710
I'm gonna try to be a little less partisan,
a little more open and a little less political

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.610
as the year comes to an end.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:05.750
I think I do a pretty decent job of being
fair and open minded in general, but a touch

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.720
more of those traits never hurt, especially
around holiday time.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.849
Politics is important, but it isn't more important
than finding some room in your life to be

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:19.200
grateful, decent and tolerant.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.569
My challenge, if you're up for it, is to perhaps
try being a little more tolerant yourself

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:26.239
in the spirit of the season.

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:31.249
I know you're intellectual opponents and sometimes
even friends and family members often won't

00:02:31.249 --> 00:02:37.000
make it easy, but I think it'll be worth the
effort as we wind down this crazy year.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.459
Whether we like it or not, we're in this thing
together and perhaps putting out some brush

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:45.930
fires now will spare us from some major fires
in the future...

